  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nAn EMS host had synchrotrons go into a state where they didn't return events. Where \"return events\", I don't have the full data on what was returned in the sync calls, if anything, since the component doing the sync is an automated monitoring C2S compoent (Matrixmon).\r\n\r\nThe bot sent events to a room successfully\r\n\r\n> 2022-06-06 06:40:44,120 - synapse.access.http.8009 - 427 - INFO - PUT-87019- 13.51.61.11 - 8009 - {@bot:domain.tld} Processed request: 0.047sec/0.001sec (0.012sec, 0.000sec) (0.002sec/0.004sec/5) 59B 200 \"PUT /_matrix/client/r0/rooms/!roomid:domain.tld/send/m.room.message/m1649849205.03078?access_token=%3Credacted%3E HTTP/1.1\" \"Net::Async::Matrix\" [0 dbevts]\r\n\r\nThe returning sync was also 200, but events we were looking for were not found in the response\r\n\r\n> 2022-06-06 06:40:57,500 - synapse.access.http.8009 - 427 - INFO - GET-3635901- 13.51.61.11 - 8009 - {@bot:domain.tld} Processed request: 0.010sec/0.000sec (0.000sec, 0.004sec) (0.000sec/0.001sec/1) 396B 200 \"GET /_matrix/client/r0/sync?access_token=<redacted>&timeout=30000&since=s809465_9626504_49106_520536_1131215_1727_1236772_62810_1 HTTP/1.1\" \"Net::Async::Matrix\" [0 dbevts]\r\n\r\nCouldn't spot anything weird in synchrotron logs. Restarted the synchrotrons and now things work as they should.\r\n\r\nWill link internal issue with customer name.\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: EMS cloud customer\r\n\r\n- **Version**: v1.57.1\r\n\r\n- **Install method**: Docker\r\n",
